<title>BELGIUM: Sabena to fly to Beirut from May 18.</title>
<headline>Sabena to fly to Beirut from May 18.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian national airline Sabena said on Monday it would start flying directly from Brussels to Beirut from May 18.</p>
<p>&quot;The economic reconstruction of this important city in the Middle East has prompted Sabena to serve this city,&quot; Sabena said in a statement.</p>
<p>It noted that Swissair, which has a 49.5 percent stake in the Belgian carrier, already flies three times a week to Beirut from Zurich.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
